"mHX" = (
/obj/structure/table/wood,
/obj/structure/fluff/statue/small{
	pixel_y = 18;
	name = "'Elven Charm'";
	desc = "This particular statue is strangely enough looking towards the Stern of the ship, rather than the sea afore as is customary. The sailor's tale goes that the Vis-Count that originally commisoned this fine vessel did so as a means of impressing a particularly beautiful Elven Baroness. Sadly for the protagonist of this tale, his chosen had rejected him, and his.. many advances. And so, as an attempt at soothing his now-broken heart, the Vis-Count ordered the statue be turned towards the Stern, so that he may always gaze upon the beauty of the Baroness. ...With tyme howeer this turned out to be a wrong choice as the ever-present, stony gaze of his would-be beloved only stopped the wound that rended his heart apart from ever healing, and so the poor Vis-Count, unable to endure the sight of that which he would never have, tossed himself one fateful dae into the Abyssor's cold embrace."
	},
/turf/open/floor/rogue/ruinedwood,
/area/rogue)
